# Bulwark Webmail 1.19.1 standalone tarball SHA-256.
# Source: https://github.com/bulwarkmail/webmail/releases/tag/1.19.1
#   asset: bulwark-standalone-1.19.1-linux-amd64.tar.gz
# Captured 2026-11-01 from the GitHub release artifact; matches the release's
# own .sha256 file and the digest GitHub publishes for the asset.
# 1.13 - 1.19.1 carry upstream security fixes in several releases (see the
# "Security" sections of its changelog), among them sanitizing re-opened
# drafts in 1.17.2. 1.18.0 and later work with Stalwart 0.16 and 1.0.
# From 1.11.1 a
# mailbox impersonation runs on an 8-hour app password Bulwark creates on the
# mailbox, instead of carrying the Stalwart master password in the cookie.
#
# Bulwark ships a prebuilt "standalone" Next.js tarball (server.js +
# node_modules + .next), so we no longer git-clone + `npm ci` +
# `npm run build`. install_bulwark() downloads this tarball, verifies
# the SHA below, and extracts it.
#
# To re-capture on a version bump (BOTH the version in install.sh AND this
# checksum must change together — a version bump alone fails SHA verification):
#   curl -sSL https://github.com/bulwarkmail/webmail/releases/download/<v>/bulwark-standalone-<v>-linux-amd64.tar.gz | sha256sum
# Paste the returned 64-char hex below. install.sh `_die`s if the
# placeholder PLACEHOLDER_CAPTURE_ON_FIRST_DEPLOY survives.
951bb557c0cff4ee62f423ff5f0971680b19810118c5e71d061b5d732130b47e
